invariant: INV-16
file: x25519_wide_table.h
catches: x25519_equiv_test
reason: one word of one entry of the table of multiples of the base point
  is off by one: y + x of 7 * 256^17 * B, entry [17][6]. The key
  generation reads it for one digit value at two of 64 positions, so a
  random scalar is wrong about one time in eight and no published vector
  need notice. bin/x25519_equiv_test reads every entry of the table and its
  negative on scalars of one nonzero digit, against both ladders.

